 - Prevents endless todo lists from accumulating
 - Configurable via Account/Board settings
 
+### Storage usage
+
+Accounts and boards report the file storage they use through `#bytes_used`. Only card images and the files embedded in board descriptions, card descriptions and comments count:
+
+- Usage is cached per board in `storage_usages` and always calculated in the background — reads never calculate, so they stay cheap no matter how many attachments a board has
+- Attachments coming and going flag the affected board and schedule a single calculation for it, so bursts of uploads from many people collapse into one calculation
+- An account's usage is the sum of its boards'
+- Models in `app/models/storage/`, framework hooks in `lib/rails_ext/storage_usage_tracking.rb`
+
 ### UUID Primary Keys
 
 All tables use UUIDs (UUIDv7 format, base36-encoded as 25-char strings):
